# TLS front for the UAT suite: https://localhost:3000 → the standalone Next server on the host.
#
# Session cookies are `__Host-`/Secure, so browsers (WebKit above all) only keep them over HTTPS;
# `tls internal` issues a local certificate, which Playwright accepts via ignoreHTTPSErrors.
#
# Upstream keep-alive must stay SHORTER than Node's HTTP keepAliveTimeout (5 s). Otherwise Caddy
# can reuse a socket Node has just closed; a POST (e.g. sign-in) on that socket fails with EOF,
# and because POST is not retried, the browser receives a bare 502.
#
# Docker Desktop's container→host hop (host.docker.internal) can stall a new connection for a
# few seconds under load. A failed dial means the request was never sent, so retrying it is safe
# even for POST: `lb_try_duration` keeps re-dialling within the window, and a short
# `dial_timeout` fits several attempts into it, instead of answering the browser with a bare 502.
#
# The same hop has also dropped out for most of a minute, cutting off requests already sent
# (EOF) as well as new dials. A request that failed after it was sent is retried only when
# repeating it is harmless (`lb_retry_match`: GET, HEAD and the idempotent PUT); a POST is never
# resent, since it may already have reached the app (an OTP could go out twice).
#
# The upstream defaults to the Docker host; set UAT_UPSTREAM to bypass that hop entirely with a
# Caddy running on the host itself.
#
# Run from frontend/ — in Docker (as CI does):
#   docker run -d --name veriprops-uat-tls -p 3000:3000 \
#     -v "$(pwd)/e2e/tls/Caddyfile:/etc/caddy/Caddyfile:ro" caddy:2-alpine
# or natively, with no container→host hop:
#   UAT_UPSTREAM=localhost:3001 caddy run --config e2e/tls/Caddyfile

localhost:3000 {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy {$UAT_UPSTREAM:host.docker.internal:3001} {
		lb_try_duration 15s
		lb_try_interval 250ms
		lb_retry_match {
			method GET HEAD PUT
		}
		transport http {
			dial_timeout 3s
			keepalive 2s
		}
	}
}
